<title>UK: FORECAST - Reuters foreign exchange poll - April.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Reuters foreign exchange poll - April.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The dollar is expected to lose ground against the yen, slipping from current levels during April, before accelerating lower thereafter, according to a Reuter poll of 34 banks and financial institutions from across the globe, conducted on April 3 and 4.</p>
<p>The average of the forecasts were as follows,</p>
<p>			   1-MTH	3-MTH	6-MTH	 12-MTH</p>
<p>    STERLING/DOLLAR  1.6303     1.6150     1.6035	1.6096</p>
<p>    DOLLAR/MARK	1.6810     1.6830     1.6835	1.6482</p>
<p>    DOLLAR/YEN	 122.42     122.06     120.49	116.72</p>
<p>Using the dollar forecasts above, the cross rates calculate at:--</p>
<p>			    1-MTH	3-MTH	6-MTH	12-MTH</p>
<p>    STERLING/MARK     2.7405     2.7181     2.6995     2.6528</p>
<p>    MARK/YEN	    72.82	72.52	71.57	70.82</p>
<p>At 0900 GMT sterling/dollar was trading at $1.6305/15, dollar/mark at 1.6940/45 and dollar/yen at 124.65/75. Sterling/mark was at 2.7640/50 and mark/yen at 73.55/60.</p>
<p>The minimum and maximum forecasts were as follows --</p>
<p>    STERLING/DOLLAR  1-mth	3-mth	6-mth	 12-mth</p>
<p>    MINIMUM	    1.6000     1.5500     1.5500	1.4900</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	    1.6850     1.6800     1.7000	1.7500</p>
<p>DOLLAR/MARK</p>
<p>    MINIMUM	    1.6320     1.5100     1.5500	1.5000</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	    1.7400     1.8000     1.8000	1.8000</p>
<p>DOLLAR/YEN</p>
<p>    MINIMUM	    118.00     113.00     110.00	105.00</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	    125.50     129.00     132.00	130.00</p>
<p>On average the forecasters expect dollar/yen to trade at 122.42 yen one month from now, easing to 122.06 in three months time before continuing its decline to trade at 116.72 in one year from now. The lowest dollar/yen is expected to fall during this period is 105.00 yen, a level unseen since May 1996.</p>
<p>The dollar is also expected to make some losses against the mark over the next month to trade at 1.6810. It is then expected to pick up, rising to 1.6830 in three months and 1.6835 in six months before settling as low as 1.6482 in a year from now.</p>
<p>The lowest dollar/mark is expected to fall during this period is 1.5000 marks and the highest it is expected to rise is 1.8000 marks.</p>
<p>Sterling is expected to make some progress during April rising to $1.6303 one month from now before reversing, slipping to $1.6150 in three months time.</p>
<p>This decline is then expected to accelerate,  falling to $1.6035 in six months and $1.6096 a year from now. The lowest sterling is expected to fall during this period is $1.4900.</p>
<p>The poll showed sterling/mark and mark/yen steadily slipping from current levels throughout the next 12 months.</p>
<p>Ranking s of the 34 forecasters by the accuracy of their one-month forecasts will be published in the first week of May, just before the results of the next poll.</p>
